<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore bunkers quiet in listless trade.</title>
<headline>Singapore bunkers quiet in listless trade.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Singapore bunker market was quiet on Friday amid scarce enquiries, traders said.</p>
<p>A lack of fresh market-inspiring factors and unchanged fundamentals kept players on the sidelines, tarders said.</p>
<p>Bunker 380-cst supplies were quoted at about $100 per tonne and the 180-cst grade was offered $3/$4 per tonne higher.</p>
<p>MDO and gas oil were at around $160/$165 and $173/$178 per tonne respectively, traders said.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (65-870 3571)</p>
